course: dictionary
lesson: 10060
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find out which one is meant. «Tết is the biggest festival in Vietnam, and families cook special food together.» The words festival, Vietnam and families are clues that Tết is a celebration.
explain: Some words look or sound like words you know, or come from other languages. «La tête» is French and means head: the ê sounds like "eh", so it is said "tet". It is not the same word as Tết, so do not mix them up.
explain: Check the clues. Tết has a capital letter and a hat over the ê, and it is a name for a festival. Tet with no marks can also be the name of a letter in the Hebrew alphabet, so look at the rest of the sentence before you decide.
fact: Tết (Tet) is the Vietnamese Lunar New Year, the most important festival in Vietnam.
fact: It is held in late January or February, when families visit each other, eat special food and give red envelopes of lucky money.
fact: Tết is a Vietnamese word, and it is used in English when we talk about this festival.
fact: Tet is also the name of a letter in the Hebrew alphabet, written ט and also called «teth».
fact: «La tête» is French and means head, so it is not a Vietnamese or Hebrew word.
exercise: Which festival is held in Vietnam in late January or February? | *Tết | Diwali | Halloween | Bonfire Night
exercise: What do families give each other at Tết to bring good luck? | Football tickets | Snow shovels | *Red envelopes of lucky money | Birthday cards
exercise: Tet is also the name of a letter in which alphabet? | Japanese | Greek | Russian | *Hebrew
test: «La tête» is French. What does it mean? | *Head | Hand | Heart | Hat
test: «Families visit each other at Tết and eat special food.» What is Tết? | *A festival in Vietnam | A letter of the alphabet | A type of sport | A French word for hat
exam: In «Tết holiday», the capital letter tells you Tết is a name. What is the best way to check your meaning of an unknown word? | Guess the first meaning in the dictionary and stop | Ask someone to pronounce it for you | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Read only the title and skip the sentence
